   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "compromising",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "compromising"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final rules require strict incident reporting (S1) and give customers per-model test results without public disclosure (S2), but S2's 8% failure limit and lack of sales stop are weakened relative to the safe standard. S3's 24-month new-unit shut-off deadline is weakened (safe is from adoption, acceptable ≤12 months), though the 6-year retrofit is acceptable. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months (acceptable), and S5 mandates recall at 8 per 100k with corrective remedies and prompt notices (acceptable). Overall the deal respects all red lines but favours Northwind."
